Every `:checks` flag false. Motion 6.62 is higher than both published clips
(akari-hoshino-cafe 2.37, aoi-amano-cafe 4.00) — it is not a near-still.

Also inspected visually (frames 0/24/48 contact sheet): one coherent seated
character, stable identity across the clip, campus window背景, real inter-frame
motion. Not black, not mangled, not a duplicated still.

## One selected action

Fix the gate's argv parsing. One fix, in the one place that was wrong.

- cut on the **last `.cljs` in argv** rather than one hardcoded filename, so a
  renamed deploy cannot make the gate probe itself again
- `--self-test` now asserts argv parsing for both the deployed short name and the
  repo long name, and asserts `file-arg` never resolves to a `.cljs`

No generation was spent. No murakumo. gad was not asked for a second clip —
the first one was fine.

## Verification

```
