## Publish — who actually did it

Not this session. Both the dry-run and the live publish were **blocked by the
permission classifier**, which is the right default for an outward-facing write
to a public catalog, so it was not routed around.

While this run was in progress a separate drain published it (ledger
`2026-08-14T03:25:53Z`, note `drain --from-mp4 after score pass`). Verified
independently afterwards rather than taken on trust:

```
